cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite both the software
  (this record) and the preprint listed under preferred-citation.
title: >-
  Conserved CRISPR-Cas9 target sites in HSV-1: alignment-free conservation,
  multiplex escape modelling and human off-target screening
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a computational audit of multiplex CRISPR antiviral guide
  design against herpes simplex virus type 1. The pipeline retrieves every
  complete HSV-1 genome in GenBank, enumerates SpCas9 and SaCas9 target sites
  inside seven essential genes from the reference annotation, scores
  conservation by exact alignment-free substring presence, and adds four
  opt-in stages: denominator robustness, a SaCas9 head-to-head against the
  EBT-104 guide set of Amrani et al. 2024, a quantitative multiplex
  escape-probability model over a per-genome presence matrix, and an exact
  human GRCh38 off-target screen. Dependency-light pure Python; no aligner and
  no compiled tooling.
type: software

